c messaging - forums, e-mails, chats, etc..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's still more about reinforcing their narrow &quot;trickster&quot; archetype than it is about making a habitat in the between-spaces of human population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:01:05-07:00","id":906497,"title":"","content":"I'm all for them taking on vine gnawer traits. Definently somethjng a Coywolf shift should have","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-03T10:09:43-07:00","id":906508,"title":"","content":"Well, could always create a new aspect of Coyote and make that one of the benifits...give them some form of access to Gnawer or urban based gifts? Granted Nuwisha already have access to homid gifts (well the homid born do). Most of these have to deal with people, and technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:12:31-07:00","id":908613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/900077-coywolf-conversion?p=906118#post906118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that a coywolf shifter has some interesting potential, particularly for diversifying the options for playing a &quot;coyote.&quot; The Nuwisha have always struck me as being very one-note. Where is the martial power associated with them in Mesoamerican folklore? Where is the adaptability they exhibit making their habitat in populated areas? These are things I wish were better represented in the text of Gaian coyotes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. No folklore, since the earliest known coywolves were sighted in 1919. So totem custody is up for grabs.<br /> 2. Hell yeah. Both coywolves and urban coyotes are adapted to urban life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T14:13:51-07:00","id":908615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/900077-coywolf-conversion?p=906508#post906508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, could always create a new aspect of Coyote and make that one of the benifits...give them some form of access to Gnawer or urban based gifts? Granted Nuwisha already have access to homid gifts (well the homid born do). Most of these have to deal with people, and technology.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking about mixing all the tech gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T12:33:16-07:00","id":910248,"title":"","content":"Oriens - Two families becomes one.<br /> <br /> As North America is ravaged by the wolf hunts, Gaia adapted. The remaining wolves in the Canadian east and Northeastern United States have gotten to fear the human hunters. From the southwest coyotes moved east, filling the roll the wolves had. Over time the two have crossed paths, amongst them the Kinfolk of both Garou and Nuwisha, the packs of wolves and coyotes worked together and eventually mated. The Kinfolk who were pregnant gave birth to a hybrid of both species, Canis Oriens. Bigger than the common coyote, yet smaller than the grey wolf. The first of the Oriens were sighted in the year 1919, yet still Kinfolk. It took a few more years and even Oriens taking their own mates to have a true breed shifter. The physical characteristics looks either like a giant Nuwisha or a smaller Garou. They were thought of mockeries but Theurges learnt that they were naturally born, not a trick of the Wyrm or the Weaver's newest child. The Oriens couldn't be labeled as outcast since their origins came from Garou and Nuwisha Kinfolk, not even the ancestor spirits are sure if Wolf or Coyote would take these children under their patronage. Wolf and Coyote decided to claim them as grand children, they will have to forge their own path with the knowledge and wisdom of their grand parent spirits to merely guide them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T15:53:22-07:00","id":939837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/speaking-of-science/wp/2016/07/29/it-turns-out-the-united-states-has-just-one-true-species-of-wolf/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/speaking-of-science/wp/2016/07/29/it-turns-out-the-united-states-has-just-one-true-species-of-wolf/\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/speaking-of-science/wp/2016/07/29/it-turns-out-the-united-states-has-just-one-true-species-of-wolf/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.washingtonpost.com/news/speaking-of-science/wp/2016/07/29/it-turns-out-the-united-states-has-just-one-true-species-of-wolf/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Something I just read and was not sure how many others who post here knew the case for the Eastern Wolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T16:02:03-07:00","id":939840,"title":"","content":"Red Wolves have large amounts of coyote blood. The Mokole pay 1 bonus point to be Samo-Bito Kin, so I would suggest charging that for a mortal (animal or human) to be a second type of Kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T08:01:06-07:00","id":959817,"title":"","content":"I can understand charging the bonus point for having a Mokole be kin to Samo-Bito. Your a lizard who's also related to a fish. Wolves and Coyotes are still in the Canis family, enough differences to seperate the two and still closely related enough to interbreed and produce offspring. If I were to put a merit or flaw, I would have it to where you can take on Garou Auspices or strictly unaligned like the Nuwisha.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:55:37-07:00","id":959940,"title":"","content":"Or you can just remove the Nuwisha as a separate Fera completely, and have them be a multi-Tribal Camp (started as solely Pure Lands, but has expanded these days) of mostly Ragabash, that don't care about traditional Purebreed but part of their deal with Coyote for their more extensive than normal Camp Gifts and Rites is that they only breed with wild coyotes. Now that coyotes fall into the species Garou can naturally mate with and produce kin/more Garou, there's no reason to worry about how much interbreeding has occurred in a given population, or what humans label them as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T15:31:06-07:00","id":960050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/900077-coywolf-conversion?p=959940#post959940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can just remove the Nuwisha as a separate Fera completely, and have them be a multi-Tribal Camp (started as solely Pure Lands, but has expanded these days) of mostly Ragabash, that don't care about traditional Purebreed but part of their deal with Coyote for their more extensive than normal Camp Gifts and Rites is that they only breed with wild coyotes. Now that coyotes fall into the species Garou can naturally mate with and produce kin/more Garou, there's no reason to worry about how much interbreeding has occurred in a given population, or what humans label them as.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In doing this, would you get rid of their lack of Rage and immunity to silver then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T16:53:51-07:00","id":960101,"title":"","content":"Yes, though I'd make sure some of the Gifts to mitigate those two are part of their Camp list for people that feel that's important to their concept (I personally don't, but I can see the argument).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T08:18:48-07:00","id":969923,"title":"","content":"Was thinking about limiting Rage and having some vulnerability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}